  "body": "## What changed\nA user post that declares `wireEdm = true` now serves Wire EDM when it has no explicit `serves` list.\nThe inferred wire dialect serves only Wire EDM.\nAn explicit `serves` list still controls the machine kinds.\n\n## Cause\nThe posting door checked the turning capability mask but ignored the engine's wire manifest flag.\nIt refused every unregistered wire script without a `serves` declaration.\n\n## Tests\n`posting::serves::tests::user_wire_manifest_serves_only_wire_edm` failed before the fix and passes after it.\n`posting::serves::tests::user_wire_manifest_keeps_explicit_serves_restriction` passes.\n`posting::serves::tests::cutting_user_script_is_refused_on_wire_edm_by_name` passes.\nReplacing production with upstream code makes the acceptance pin fail.\nRestoring the fix makes all three pins pass.\nChanging the wire branch to accept every kind makes the exclusivity pin fail on Mill.\nRestoring the kind check makes all three pins pass.\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed with zero failures.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\nNo physical EDM or interactive picker was exercised.\nThe new pins exercise the posting admission and refusal functions directly.\n\n## Overlaps\nNo open PR touched the changed source, test, or decision paths at the overlap check.\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: Honor a user post script's wireEdm manifest when admitting Wire EDM posts.\n\nFixes #1335\n",
